  "2026-07-25T22:35:02.712Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: added public CLI-contract to extension-flag adapter, exported list/search baselines, migrated pm-search-advanced through the first-party runtime bridge, and passed 158 focused unit/integration tests plus targeted ESLint."
  "2026-07-25T22:38:02.233Z","harness:codex","Contract evidence: full CLI contract snapshot stayed current; SDK surface update classified eight additive exports across sdk, sdk/authoring, and sdk/runtime with no breaking or changed symbols."
  "2026-07-25T23:27:32.158Z","harness:codex","Evidence: canonical SDK search flag definitions exposed a real package-runtime compatibility edge because list flags arrive as Commander string arrays. Extended readCsvListOption to normalize arrays and legacy CSV scalars, updated search-advanced to consume it, and restored fresh-snapshot installation plus projected search output. Full sandboxed coverage passed: 371 files, 6,388 tests, 100% statements (44,024/44,024), branches (31,232/31,232), functions (9,002/9,002), and lines (42,766/42,766)."
  "2026-07-25T23:33:31.410Z","harness:codex","Acceptance evidence: packed the current checkout, installed it into an unrelated /var/tmp consumer, verified the resolved binary points inside that consumer package, initialized an isolated tracker, generated both package-init and extension-init artifacts, installed their local packed SDK dependency, passed each generated typecheck and node:test suite, installed both artifacts, invoked `pm agent workflow ping` and `pm agent hooks ping`, imported the public SDK authoring surface (57 canonical search definitions), and passed isolated deep strict package doctor."
  "2026-07-25T23:36:13.416Z","harness:codex","Scope status before PR: the canonical flag adapter, list-array runtime coercion, public authoring exports, and first-party search migration are complete and fully verified. The separate acceptance clause to replace remaining first-party PM_CLI_PACKAGE_ROOT loader copies is intentionally still outstanding in this same canonical item; this item must remain active through review and return to open after this PR rather than being falsely closed."
  "2026-07-25T23:43:46.607Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/718 at head 46707ab7 completed all required CI gates: four coverage shards plus 100% aggregate coverage, static/typecheck/compat/smoke gates, Windows and macOS regression, Node 22/24 runtime smoke, benchmarks, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, CodeFactor, DeepScan, docs, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, and actionlint. Thread-aware review inventory found zero inline threads or actionable findings; CodeRabbit and Sourcery returned quota notices, CodSpeed reported an environment-mismatched 0.01% informational signal while the repository benchmark gate passed, and Codecov confirmed every modified coverable line is covered."
